mothershipOS: a scanout flush's fence completes when the compositor shows the frame (its Wayland frame callback),
not at once. The guest's page flip then completes when its frame is on screen, so the buffer it showed before is
free: real back pressure and vblank pacing for the guest (crosvm said "there is no good way to apply back pressure
to the guest gpu driver right now"), and zero-copy scanout of guest buffers without the guest drawing into the frame
being scanned out. Needs a guest that fences its flushes (PixelOS: virtio_gpu.ko patch) and a compositor that sends
frame callbacks only once a frame is shown (mship-presenter). A fence waits at most 100 ms; a surface with every
frame callback slot taken counts frames as done at once.

